  "review": {
    "book": "JDG",
    "entityID": "person:canaan_914",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "After the death of Joshua, the children of Israel asked of the LORD, saying, “Who should go up for us first against the Canaanites, to fight against them?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "Judah said to Simeon his brother, “Come up with me into my lot, that we may fight against the Canaanites; and I likewise will go with you into your lot.” So Simeon went with him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:4",
        "textualBasisJa": "Judah went up, and the LORD delivered the Canaanites and the Perizzites into their hand. They struck ten thousand men in Bezek."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "They found Adoni-Bezek in Bezek, and they fought against him. They struck the Canaanites and the Perizzites."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "After that, the children of Judah went down to fight against the Canaanites who lived in the hill country, and in the South, and in the lowland."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "Judah went against the Canaanites who lived in Hebron. (The name of Hebron before that was Kiriath Arba.) They struck Sheshai, Ahiman, and Talmai."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "Judah went with Simeon his brother, and they struck the Canaanites who inhabited Zephath, and utterly destroyed it. The name of the city was called Hormah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:27",
        "textualBasisJa": "Manasseh didn’t drive out the inhabitants of Beth Shean and its towns, nor Taanach and its towns, nor the inhabitants of Dor and its towns, nor the inhabitants of Ibleam and its towns, nor the inhabitants of Megiddo and its towns; but the Canaanites would dwell in that land."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Israel had grown strong, they put the Canaanites to forced labor, and didn’t utterly drive them out."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:29",
        "textualBasisJa": "Ephraim didn’t drive out the Canaanites who lived in Gezer, but the Canaanites lived in Gezer among them."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:30",
        "textualBasisJa": "Zebulun didn’t drive out the inhabitants of Kitron, nor the inhabitants of Nahalol; but the Canaanites lived among them, and became subject to forced labor."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "but the Asherites lived among the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land, for they didn’t drive them out."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:33",
        "textualBasisJa": "Naphtali didn’t drive out the inhabitants of Beth Shemesh, nor the inhabitants of Beth Anath; but he lived among the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land. Nevertheless the inhabitants of Beth Shemesh and of Beth Anath became subject to forced labor."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 3:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "the five lords of the Philistines, all the Canaanites, the Sidonians, and the Hivites who lived on Mount Lebanon, from Mount Baal Hermon to the entrance of Hamath."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 3:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Israel lived among the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Amorites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites."
      }
    ],
